    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        1180,
        106
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        340
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 2,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Same analysis as the shot-based stack. Rigid grid, one tempo, zero drift.\n\nIf the picture turns over off the beat, the knobs are downbeat_offset (whole\nbeats within the bar) and phase_offset_beats (slides the whole grid, takes\nfractions). The report prints the lock score: 1.0 is chance, below 1.6 the\ngrid is not locked."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        2400,
        582
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        470
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 3,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "WHAT MAKES THIS DIFFERENT FROM THE SHOT STACK.\n\nThere, each cut is an independent clip. Here the picture is one continuous\ndiffusion and the music drives how much it moves and how tightly it holds.\n\n  energy -> motion scale     louder moves more\n  energy -> context reuse    quiet holds still, loud is free to change\n  bars   -> prompt keyframes the picture turns over on the bar\n\nAnimateDiff has no cut. hard_cuts writes each prompt index with a trailing\ncolon, which tells ADE to hold rather than interpolate: the picture turns\nover in a frame or two instead of dissolving. That is as close as it gets,\nand the crossfade is what the technique is actually good at.\n\nFRAME RATE. bar_aligned picks a generation rate that puts one bar on exactly\ncontext_length frames, so the model's attention window and the musical phrase\nare the same thing. At 121.03 BPM that is 8.07 fps and 1574 frames for the\nwhole track, against 4876 for the shot stack at 25 fps. Deliver at a higher\nrate by interpolating the assembled video, not by generating more frames."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
