      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "AnimateLCM, so few steps and low cfg: 8 steps, cfg 1.8, lcm sampler,\nsgm_uniform. The LoRA is not optional, it is what makes 8 steps work.\n\nbeta_schedule must be sqrt_linear (AnimateDiff) for an SD1.5 motion module.\n\nThe motion module itself is loaded inside the expansion, not on the canvas,\nbecause it is per-segment."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        940,
        1624
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        620
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 5,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "COHERENCE IS THE INVERSE OF ENERGY, ON PURPOSE. Context reuse holds the\npicture steady by leaning on the previous window, so it belongs in the quiet\npassages. Applying it during a loud passage fights the motion curve and gives\na video that strains without moving. Measured correlation -0.72.\n\nMOTION RANGE IS NARROW. 1.0 is the model's own amount of movement. Past about\n1.5 the motion module stops producing motion and starts producing smear.\n\nlimit renders the first N segments. 0 is the whole song. Segments are written\nto disk as they finish, so a failure late in the track does not cost the run.\n\ndecode_batch is where this stack runs out of memory, not sampling. A whole\nsegment of frames decoded at once is the thing that will not fit."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
